; Provider-route executable family, 4 of 7 — absence, made loud.
;
; The schema is well-formed and the provider resolves; there is simply no
; implementation behind it on any host. The tempting behaviour is to skip
; the check and pass, which would make a document validate differently
; depending on how its validator was built. Instead the bucket is
; poisoned exactly as a refusal poisons it, and one diagnostic says so.
;
; The two references are unchecked, not accepted and not rejected —
; `u_res` is deliberately not among the names the source would have
; yielded, and it is still silent. A host that reported it would be
; claiming to know a member set it never computed.
(use-plugin "lines")

(shader :name main :src "u_time")

(bind :uniform u_time)
(bind :uniform u_res)
